      {
        "id": "kestrel-overnight",
        "heading": "One night on battery: a low-battery alert before dawn, and a package alert that can arrive late",
        "text": [
          "Based on the Kestrel Porch Cam design. The story runs from Thursday night to Friday morning; clock minutes are illustrative. The camera checks in with the Kestrel cloud every 30 minutes, and the phone shows what the last check-in said.",
          "Battery figures follow the design: about 1% an hour at rest and about 1% per recorded clip. The morning solar charging rate (3.5% an hour) is an illustrative midpoint of the design's 3–4%. At the design's figures the battery would reach 20% nearer 2:30 AM. This story keeps the 4 AM alert time instead, so the battery gauge holds at 25% until the 4:00 AM check-in. Check-ins the phone shows between steps (1:00 AM, 6:30 AM, 8:00 AM) are illustrative."
        ],
